@*
    TELLS A SPACE-SCOPED PAGE THAT SpaceArrival HAS ANSWERED - story 4.4, ledger deferred-work.md:550, open question 15 (a).

    Rendered inside SpaceArrival's content, so it first renders only once the Space has answered; the page's own first
    render was an earlier browser task. Space home writes its narration then, into the status region it rendered empty on
    its first render, so assistive technology hears a CHANGE to a live region rather than a region inserted already
    holding its sentence (the LiveAnnouncement rule: regions are empty from the first render). Renders nothing.
*@

@code {
    /// <summary>Raised once, after this first renders.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnArrived { get; set; }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender) =>
        firstRender ? OnArrived.InvokeAsync() : Task.CompletedTask;
}
